<title>AUSTRALIA: Rundle twins have Stuart funds ready.</title>
<headline>Rundle twins have Stuart funds ready.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Rundle shale oil twins, Southern Pacific Petroleum Nl and Central Pacific Minerals, said on Tuesday they now had the funding in place to start building stage one of the Stuart oil project.</p>
<p>The announcement followed the receipt by their brokers of formal acceptances for the combined placement of shares announced last week to raise A$89.95 million, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;This was the final step required by the Stuart project co-venturers, SPP/CPM and Suncor Energy, to enable them to move to Financial Close which now only involves completion of legal formalities,&quot; they said.</p>
</text>
